Aerie-Purpose: Paint the window frame with the Aerie tint: add the tint view under everything in BrowserView, let Helium's frame fills paint nothing while it is on, force the rounded page card, take the card radius from radius-xl and hide the card's outline when the theme asks for no border.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (browser_view.*, themed_background.cc, multi_contents_background_view.cc, multi_contents_view.cc, contents_container_view.cc, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/views/helium (frame_corner_radius.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #178. Helium already has the rounded frame and the page card (rounded-frame-corners.patch,
frame-background.patch, native-frame-materials.patch). This is the one hook patch that puts the
Aerie frame on top of them; the view itself (FrameTintView, its own opaque ui::Layer, painted on
state change only) and the question "is the tint on" are in the overlay,
chrome/browser/ui/views/aerie_frame, and the palette and paint in components/aerie_frame.

- browser_view.*: a normal window with the sidebar layout creates FrameTintView as its first
  child, before the main background region, so it is the lowest layer. It is created in the
  constructor, with the window, and given the contents container as the page card once that
  exists. frame_tint_view_for_testing() is for the browser tests.
- themed_background.cc: PaintBackground() paints nothing for the frame colour while the tint is on.
  CustomCornersBackground (the sidebar's column, the corners) and MultiContentsBackgroundView all
  paint the frame colour through it. The toolbar colour is not touched: split view's mini toolbar
  and the side panel still need it.
- multi_contents_background_view.cc: the gutter around the card is the tint, so while it is on the
  view is a transparent textured layer, as it is with native frame materials.
- multi_contents_view.cc: the rounded frame is on whatever kHeliumRoundedFrame says, so the
  page is always in a card.
- contents_container_view.cc: the card's outline is hidden when the theme's card-border token is
  0 px (Vivid). A theme that asks for a border keeps Helium's one-pixel stroke until slice I
  (themes) gives it the token colour and width.
- frame_corner_radius.cc: GetGenericFrameRadius() and GetPaddedFrameRadius() both return
  radius-xl (14), so the card, the side panel and the drop target agree.
- BUILD.gn: the deps those need.


